    "verdict": "BEST-INTERVENTION multi-axis score (transparent, equal-weighted synthesis of the validated axes druggability + breadth + resistance-robustness + condition-robustness; host-safety is a hard upstream filter). Ranked 49 nominated targets. Top: murB, murG, dxr, murF, ispE, mraY. VALIDATION (vs experimental essentiality, PREDVAL, the only truth axis available): Spearman(score, #organisms-experimentally-essential) = 0.6896 (p=0.0); top-quartile targets are experimentally essential in 2.583 organisms on average vs 1.135 for the rest -> the score DOES rank experimentally-real targets higher. Consistency: menC (flagged weak by PREDVAL+SYNLETH+CONDROB) ranks 35/49 (near the bottom). **HONEST BOUNDS (falsify-first): (1) DECISION-SUPPORT synthesis, NOT a validated predictor of clinical/drug success \u2014 no ground-truth of 'best intervention' exists to fit against, so weights are EQUAL by design (fitting would fabricate confidence). (2) The Spearman-0.69 validation is only PARTLY INDEPENDENT: two of the four axes (resistance, condition-robustness) are FBA-essentiality-DERIVED and the truth axis is EXPERIMENTAL essentiality, so the correlation partly re-expresses the already-validated essentiality signal (VAL-ESS); the genuinely-independent contributions are druggability + breadth. So this confirms the composite orders targets sensibly and does not destroy the essentiality signal \u2014 it is not an independent oracle. (3) A few bottom ranks (e.g. HP_0740, ribA1) are UNMAPPED-AXIS artifacts (locus-tag genes with no resistance/condition class -> R=C=0 -> artificially low), not genuinely poor targets. Axes are cross-organism/ortholog-transferred; hypotheses; not wet-lab.**",
